<section image-layout="blank" id="BXIZ3SSShi" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="qls7Vu29yQ"><display size="md" font-size="50pt">A perfect plan can only deliver<br/><span text-color="accent">what it already knows</span></display><spacer mode="fixed" size="18pt"/><grid divider="sm neutral-border"><grid-item id="AuoJBBTJN4" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Efficiency</p><p font-size="lg">Standardized execution reduces variation when the destination is known. Applied too early, it can erase the evidence discovery needs.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="PBMVRhi4A1" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">The creative paradox</p><p font-size="lg">We need enough structure to act, with enough openness to encounter something we did not prescribe.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>